@*
    OdsLineChart — the axis'd trend card (Odyssey Design System · components/LineChart).
    Unlike OdsSparkline (compact, axis-less), this is the full card: a head (title · sub
    on the left, headline figure + optional delta on the right) over an SVG line/area plot
    with horizontal gridlines and value / category axis labels. Backs the Dashboard
    net-worth chart and the Tax Statements overview.

    Series is OdsLinePoint[] (oldest → newest); points with a null Value are skipped.
    Format formats the headline + axis numbers (a money formatter); AxisFormat overrides
    the y-axis ticks with a compact variant. Cumulative plots the running total. ShowDelta
    adds a latest-vs-first delta (mint up / coral down) with DeltaSuffix text. One point
    renders as a dot; an empty series renders the EmptyLabel.

    A reconstructed series (the dashboard's net-worth history) needs three things a plain
    trend card does not, and all three are additive — a series of plain Normal points with
    a non-negative domain renders exactly as it did before:
      • NEGATIVES. The value domain drops below zero when it has to. The area then anchors
        at Sy(0) rather than the plot floor and a labelled zero gridline is drawn. A domain
        that never goes negative keeps the floor-anchored fill and the four even gridlines.
      • POINT KINDS, not a flag: Normal (measured) · Partial (understated — a contributing
        account had no exchange rate) · Revalued (a real step, an estimate took effect).
        Shape and stroke carry the meaning, never fill colour: filled dot · hollow dot with
        dashed adjoining segments · filled dot with a vertical tick. A Partial ENDPOINT
        suppresses the delta; a Revalued one does not.
      • A TEXT EQUIVALENT — TextEquivalent renders a visually-hidden table of every point
        and its state. Opt-in, so existing consumers' assistive-tech output is unchanged.

    Sub is a RenderFragment, so a consumer can hand it note sentences rather than one
    caption string (the DS contract already types sub as a node).

    The parameters and the plot geometry live in OdsLineChart.razor.cs.

    Pure SVG + tokens (default stroke --chart-1) so it re-themes light/dark. Styled by
    .odc-lc / .odc-line-svg in the global sheet.
*@

<div class="@($"odc-lc{(string.IsNullOrEmpty(Class) ? "" : " " + Class)}")">
    <div class="odc-lc-head">
        <div>
            @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(Title))
            {
                <div class="odc-lc-ttl">@Title</div>
            }
            @if (Sub is not null)
            {
                <div class="odc-lc-sub">@Sub</div>
            }
        </div>
        @if (Figure is not null || _pts.Count > 0)
        {
            <div class="odc-lc-figure">
                <div class="odc-lc-num">@(Figure ?? Format((decimal)_pts[^1].Value))</div>
                @if (_deltaOk)
                {
                    var delta = _pts[^1].Value - _pts[0].Value;
                    <div class="odc-lc-delta @(delta >= 0 ? "income" : "expense")">
                        @(delta >= 0 ? "+" : "−")@Format((decimal)Math.Abs(delta))@(string.IsNullOrEmpty(DeltaSuffix) ? "" : " " + DeltaSuffix)
                    </div>
                }
            </div>
        }
    </div>

    @if (_pts.Count == 0)
    {
        <div class="odc-lc-empty">@EmptyLabel</div>
    }
    else
    {
        <svg class="odc-line-svg" viewBox="0 0 1000 252" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet"
             role="img" aria-label="@EffectiveAriaLabel">
            <g stroke="var(--chart-grid)" stroke-width="1">
                @foreach (var v in _gridVals)
                {
                    @* Zero gets its own heavier baseline below, so it is not also an ordinary gridline. *@
                    @if (v != 0)
                    {
                        <line x1="@Fmt(X0)" y1="@Fmt(Sy(v))" x2="@Fmt(X1)" y2="@Fmt(Sy(v))" />
                    }
                }
            </g>
            @* Razor reserves <text> as a control keyword, so the axis labels are
               emitted as raw SVG markup. *@
            <g class="odc-lc-axis">@((MarkupString)YAxisMarkup)</g>
            <g class="odc-lc-axis">@((MarkupString)XAxisMarkup)</g>
            @if (Area && !_single)
            {
                @if (_straddles)
                {
                    @* A straddling domain fills flat — a vertical gradient across a band that
                       crosses zero would read as a second signal. *@
                    <path d="@AreaPath" fill="@Color" fill-opacity="0.14" />
                }
                else
                {
                    <defs>
                        <linearGradient id="@_fillId" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1">
                            <stop offset="0%" stop-color="@Color" stop-opacity="0.26" />
                            <stop offset="100%" stop-color="@Color" stop-opacity="0" />
                        </linearGradient>
                    </defs>
                    <path d="@AreaPath" fill="url(#@_fillId)" />
                }
            }
            @if (_straddles)
            {
                <line class="odc-lc-zero" x1="@Fmt(X0)" y1="@Fmt(Sy(0))" x2="@Fmt(X1)" y2="@Fmt(Sy(0))" />
            }
            @if (!_single && !_anyMarked)
            {
                <polyline points="@LinePts" fill="none" stroke="@Color" stroke-width="2.4"
                          stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-linecap="round" />
            }
            @if (!_single && _anyMarked)
            {
                @* An all-Normal series keeps the polyline above, so its markup is byte-identical to
                   what it was; only a marked series pays for per-segment strokes, which is what lets
                   a dashed run show where the data is understated. *@
                for (var i = 1; i < _pts.Count; i++)
                {
                    var understated = _pts[i - 1].Kind == OdsLinePointKind.Partial
                                      || _pts[i].Kind == OdsLinePointKind.Partial;
                    <line x1="@Fmt(Sx(i - 1))" y1="@Fmt(Sy(_pts[i - 1].Value))"
                          x2="@Fmt(Sx(i))" y2="@Fmt(Sy(_pts[i].Value))"
                          stroke="@Color" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"
                          stroke-dasharray="@(understated ? "2 5" : null)" />
                }
            }
            @for (var i = 0; i < _pts.Count; i++)
            {
                var cx = Fmt(Sx(i));
                var y = Sy(_pts[i].Value);
                var r = i == _pts.Count - 1 ? 4.0 : 2.5;
                @switch (_pts[i].Kind)
                {
                    case OdsLinePointKind.Partial:
                        <circle cx="@cx" cy="@Fmt(y)" r="@Fmt(r + 1.4)" fill="var(--mud-palette-surface)"
                                stroke="@Color" stroke-width="1.8" />
                        break;
                    case OdsLinePointKind.Revalued:
                        <g>
                            <line x1="@cx" y1="@Fmt(y - 8)" x2="@cx" y2="@Fmt(y + 8)"
                                  stroke="@Color" stroke-width="1.6" />
                            <circle cx="@cx" cy="@Fmt(y)" r="@Fmt(r)" fill="@Color" />
                        </g>
                        break;
                    default:
                        <circle cx="@cx" cy="@Fmt(y)" r="@Fmt(r)" fill="@Color" />
                        break;
                }
            }
        </svg>

        @if (MarkLegend && _anyMarked)
        {
            <div class="odc-lc-marks">
                @if (_pts.Any(p => p.Kind == OdsLinePointKind.Partial))
                {
                    <span class="odc-lc-mark">
                        <svg width="26" height="10" viewBox="0 0 26 10" aria-hidden="true">
                            <line x1="0" y1="5" x2="26" y2="5" stroke="@Color" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="2 5" />
                            <circle cx="13" cy="5" r="3.6" fill="var(--mud-palette-surface)" stroke="@Color" stroke-width="1.6" />
                        </svg>
                        @PartialLabel
                    </span>
                }
                @if (_pts.Any(p => p.Kind == OdsLinePointKind.Revalued))
                {
                    <span class="odc-lc-mark">
                        <svg width="26" height="10" viewBox="0 0 26 10" aria-hidden="true">
                            <line x1="0" y1="5" x2="26" y2="5" stroke="@Color" stroke-width="2" />
                            <line x1="13" y1="0" x2="13" y2="10" stroke="@Color" stroke-width="1.6" />
                            <circle cx="13" cy="5" r="2.6" fill="@Color" />
                        </svg>
                        @RevaluedLabel
                    </span>
                }
            </div>
        }

        @if (TextEquivalent)
        {
            <table class="odc-sr-only">
                @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(Title))
                {
                    <caption>@Title</caption>
                }
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th scope="col">@TextEquivalentLabel</th>
                        <th scope="col">Value</th>
                        <th scope="col">State</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    @foreach (var p in _pts)
                    {
                        <tr>
                            <th scope="row">@p.Label</th>
                            <td>@Format((decimal)p.Value)</td>
                            <td>@KindDescription(p.Kind)</td>
                        </tr>
                    }
                </tbody>
            </table>
        }
    }
</div>
